      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "AL Ummah Community Center demonstrates high operational resilience with <cite id=\"13\">9.0 months of working capital</cite>, providing a buffer against its recent revenue volatility. Its direct service model ensures that <cite id=\"14\">food pantry and youth services</cite> are delivered personally by the organization rather than through third-party intermediaries. Furthermore, the organization has <cite id=\"15\">verified evidence and outcomes</cite> for its programs, which is a high standard for a community-based organization of its size."
      ],
      "summary": "founded in 2018, AL Ummah Community Center (AUCC) is a New Jersey-based nonprofit that operates on <cite id=\"1\">Islamic principles of public service</cite>, love, and equality. The organization provides a range of services including the <cite id=\"2\">Ummah's Kitchen Food Pantry</cite>, youth programs, and global water campaigns. In FY2024, the organization reported <cite id=\"3\">$464,660 in total revenue</cite>, which represents a significant <cite id=\"4\">67% decline from the previous year</cite> when revenue was $1,415,881. Despite this contraction, AUCC maintains a <cite id=\"5\">program expense ratio of 82.3%</cite> according to its most recent filings, though Charity Navigator notes a historical <cite id=\"6\">program expense ratio of 82.3%</cite>. The charity holds an <cite id=\"7\">overall score of 71.0/100 from Charity Navigator</cite>, reflecting a mix of strong leadership and developing accountability practices. AUCC serves as a local hub through <cite id=\"8\">Masjid Al'Nuha</cite> while also facilitating international aid in regions like <cite id=\"9\">Palestine, Syria, and Somalia</cite>.",
